    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Birds flap their wings down and back to push the air. That push moves them up and forward!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐦",
        "text": "Flap to push the air",
        "cue": "flap",
        "sub": "Up and forward!",
        "sub_cue": "forward"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "But when I flap my arms, nothing happens!",
      "punch": "nothing"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Birds have super strong chest muscles. And their wings are curved, so air rushing past gives them a lift.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Built to fly",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/muscle-1",
            "label": "Strong muscles",
            "cue": "strong"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🪶",
            "label": "Curved wings",
            "cue": "curved"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⬆️",
            "label": "Lift!",
            "cue": "lift"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What else helps?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Feathers! They are light but strong, and they make a smooth wing shape that catches the air.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🪶",
        "text": "Feathers: light and strong",
        "cue": "feathers",
        "sub": "A smooth wing shape",
        "sub_cue": "smooth"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Are birds heavy like me?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Birds are very light for their size. Many of their bones are hollow, with tiny struts inside, like little bridges.",
      "punch": "hollow",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🦴",
        "text": "Hollow bones",
        "cue": "hollow",
        "sub": "Light but strong inside",
        "sub_cue": "struts"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Do they have to flap all the time?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Not always! Big birds like eagles can glide and soar on rising warm air, hardly flapping at all.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🦅",
        "text": "Glide and soar",
        "cue": "glide",
        "sub": "Riding warm air",
        "sub_cue": "rising"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Strong wings, feathers and light bones. Birds are built to fly!",
